# Containerization Plan

## Goal
Containerize the Java Spring Boot application so it can be built and run as a Docker image for Azure or other container platforms.

## Service
- assistance
  - Language: Java 21
  - Build: Maven
  - Framework: Spring Boot
  - Entrypoint: `com.dekra.assistance.AssistanceApplication`
  - Runtime: `java -jar /app/app.jar`

## Actions Completed
1. Scanned repository and confirmed a single Maven-based Spring Boot service.
2. Generated a production-ready multi-stage `Dockerfile` at `./Dockerfile`.
3. Added `.dockerignore` to reduce build context size.

## Dockerfile Details
- Build stage uses `maven:3.9.9-eclipse-temurin-21`.
- Runtime stage uses `eclipse-temurin:21-jre-alpine`.
- Builds the Spring Boot jar with `mvn -B package -DskipTests -Dmaven.javadoc.skip=true`.
- Copies the generated fat JAR into the runtime image.
- Exposes port `8080`.
- Uses `ENTRYPOINT ["java", "-jar", "/app/app.jar"]`.

## Next Step
- Start the local Docker daemon and run:
  - `docker buildx build --platform=linux/amd64 -t assistance:latest .`

## Blocker
- Local Docker daemon is not running or not accessible from this environment.
  - `docker version` shows a working client, but it cannot connect to the Docker socket at `/Users/paolopluviano/.docker/run/docker.sock`.

